From: PS5_Proton <local>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: PS5: the DOS area stays a bare reservation

virtual_init maps 0x10000-0x110000 read-write inside Wine's reserved area, for apps that touch the DOS area without
allocating it. On PS5 VirtualQuery's walk between views asks the kernel what lies in Wine's reserved space, and since
patch 1128 an entry that does not read as a bare reservation is a mapping that is not Wine's: occupied. The read-write
DOS area is such an entry, so a 32-bit program saw no free block below 16 MiB, where it had found 16
(virtual-query32: reserved=16 on v3-jit-gatecases-2026-10-14, reserved=0 on v2-backend-gate-2026-10-15; the gap log
read "0x10000-0x110000 reads occupied: protection 0x3 type 12 flags 0x12"). It now stays a bare reservation, as all of
Wine's reserved space does; a process also keeps the 1 MiB of flexible memory it took.

Console: v3-gap-2026-10-15 measured the cause; the fix is not yet run.
---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -4862,6 +4862,12 @@
 
     /* make the DOS area accessible (except the low 64K) to hide bugs in broken apps like Excel 2003 */
     size = (char *)address_space_start - (char *)0x10000;
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    /* Not on PS5: it stays a bare reservation, as all of Wine's reserved space. Read-write, it is a mapping VirtualQuery's
+     * guard (__wine_ps5_vm_gap) cannot tell from one that is not Wine's, so the 1 MiB read as occupied
+     * ("gap 0x10000-0x110000 reads occupied: protection 0x3", v3-gap-2026-10-15-virtual-query32). */
+    size = 0;
+#endif
     if (size && mmap_is_in_reserved_area( (void*)0x10000, size ) == 1)
         anon_mmap_fixed( (void *)0x10000, size, PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE, 0 );
 #if defined(__PROSPERO__) && defined(_WIN64)
